    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GXSKz152TKYLU2Up3YFrPV)_\n\nStacked on #105 (base is its branch; retarget to `main` after it merges).\n\n## What\n\n- `sp-vulpea-split` becomes `sp-split-leave-parents`: `libraries/modules/funct/sp-split-leave-parents.el`, feature, `provide` and load warning renamed; `sp-vulpea-ext` requires the new name. Only those renames differ from the old code.\n- Its doc moves out of `sp-vulpea.org` into `sp-org-lint.org` as its own section, which tangles the separate file. The old split note is now `docs/tangles/funct/sp-split-leave-parents-old.org`.\n- `docs/main.org` module tree, the `sp-vulpea.org` table and load-order prose, the `sp-org-lint` references and the `load-order.org` dot graph (the SVGs are built from it) are updated.\n\nI read \"the global doc\" as `sp-org-lint.org`. Say so if you meant another file.\n\n## Testing\n\nBoth docs tangle cleanly and the `.el` differs from the old file only by the renames. Not loaded with vulpea/Denote (not available here); the dot graph was not rendered (no Graphviz).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01BZJ5xQsEdMUBRHcJfgXvPb)_",
